  "final_message": "The root cause was an off-by-one in `is_redeemable` in `billing/discounts.py`. It compared `times_redeemed > max_redemptions`, so a coupon with one redemption allowed and one already used still counted as redeemable. I changed `>` to `>=`.\n\nThe full suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so that run covers the existing tests only. I also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"discounts.py\", \"function\": \"is_redeemable\"}`.\n\n`subscribe` already checks `is_redeemable` before creating the subscription, so the fix applies there too. No second change was needed to stop a subscription being created with an exhausted coupon.",
